      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "While it is certainly possible to implement a single "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Validator"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " class to validate each of the nested objects in a rich object, it may be better to encapsulate the validation logic for each nested class of object in its own "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Validator"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " implementation. A simple example of a “rich” object would be a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Customer"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " that is composed of two "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "String"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " properties (a first and a second name) and a complex "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Address"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " object. "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Address"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " objects may be used independently of "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Customer"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " objects, so a distinct "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "AddressValidator"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " has been implemented. If you want your "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "CustomerValidator"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " to reuse the logic contained within the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "AddressValidator"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " class without resorting to copy-and-paste, you can dependency-inject or instantiate an "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "AddressValidator"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " within your "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "CustomerValidator"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", as the following example shows:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "dlist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
